## Coding Conventions

- Features: `data/` `domain/` `presentation/` when API exists; presentation-only is OK for local/demo features (home, discover, splash, shell, setting)
- Files: `*_page.dart`, `*_provider.dart`, `*_repository.dart` / `*_repository_impl.dart`, `*_remote_datasource.dart`, `*_local_datasource.dart`, `*_model.dart`, `*_usecase.dart`
- Models extend entities; `fromJson` / `toJson` / `fromEntity` as needed
- Constant classes: private constructor `const X._()`
- Strings: add getters on `L10n` (`_t(en, ar)`). Use `context.l10n`. Do not hardcode user-facing copy
- Layout: `Responsive.pagePadding()`, `.w/.h/.sp/.r`, `AppColors` / `context.palette`. Fonts: Inter (en), Cairo (ar) via `AppTheme`
- After mutations: `notifyListeners()`
- Repository returns `Either`; provider folds to `_errorMessage` + snackbar in UI
- Imports: `package:yalla_5roga/...`

```dart
// ✅ read vs watch
context.watch<GroupsProvider>().visible
context.read<GroupsProvider>().markRead(id)

// ✅ navigation
Get.to(() => GroupDetailsPage(groupId: group.id));

// ❌ do not call ApiClient from a widget
```

