## Modification Rules

- Always inspect existing code before creating new code.
- Reuse existing implementations whenever possible.
- Do not duplicate existing services/providers/repositories/widgets.
- Do not invent API endpoints.
- Do not invent models or architecture when an existing implementation can be reused.
- Do not place API/networking logic directly inside UI widgets.
- Follow the existing Provider implementation.
- Follow the existing architecture.
- Keep changes minimal and focused.
- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Preserve existing behavior unless the task explicitly requires changing it.
- Use existing authentication/networking mechanisms.
- Follow existing naming and coding conventions.

